kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "app-tui"
purpose: "TBD - created by archiving change c325-add-app-tui-spec. Update purpose after archive."
valid_scope[2]: src/,tests/
requirements[23]{req_id,title,statement}:
  tui1,"inline-render","The TUI MUST render inline using ratatui Viewport::Inline with Terminal::insert_before to commit finalized lines to the terminal scrollback; the TUI MUST NOT enter the alternate screen (no ?1049h). Evidence: ratatui 0.30.2 insert_before is a stable public API (ratatui-core-0.1.2/src/terminal/inline.rs:109); pi renders inline with no alt-screen (grep of packages/tui/src finds ?1049h only in external-editor cleanup); codex is inline too."
  tui2,"in-process-driver","The TUI MUST drive the agent via app::core::driver::InProcessDriver (the same Driver path as print mode); the TUI MUST NOT default to a RemoteDriver or an auto-spawned daemon. Evidence: codex AppServerTarget::Embedded is the TUI default (codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs:814-830); pi InteractiveMode holds AgentSessionRuntime directly (coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/interactive-mode.ts:265,391)."
  tui3,"three-surfaces-coexist","The rpc (stdio JSONL), server (REST+WS), and tui (inline) application surfaces MUST coexist; none MAY be removed in the name of unification. Evidence: codex keeps in-process TUI + app-server stdio (powers VSCode ext) + app-server-daemon (unix socket); pi keeps in-process TUI + --mode rpc + orchestrator serve; neither project dropped any transport."
  tui4,"reuse-contract","The TUI MUST import only crate::agent (mod-level), crate::app::core (Driver/composition), crate::protocol, and crate::domain; it MUST NOT import crate::agent::session, crate::agent::runtime, or crate::infra. Slash command semantics MUST reuse protocol::Command variants rather than inventing a parallel command vocabulary."
  tui5,"no-skeleton-spray","Every file created under src/app/tui/ MUST be driven by a real entry point (tui::run) within its own change; the TUI MUST NOT use #[allow(dead_code)] to land undriven skeleton code. Undriven skeleton is the documented root cause of the prior two failed TUI attempts."
  tui10,"repl-entry","The CLI MUST dispatch to app::tui::run when no prompt is provided and stdin is a TTY (mirroring pi resolveAppMode), entering an inline REPL driven by InProcessDriver; a --tui flag MAY force the TUI even with a prompt."
  tui11,"event-loop","The TUI MUST run a tokio::select! event loop multiplexing three sources: the XyEvent stream from Driver::run, crossterm keyboard input via EventStream (requires crossterm event-stream feature), and a cancellation signal that calls Driver::abort."
  tui12,"inline-render-pipeline","The TUI MUST render finalized content to the scrollback via Terminal::insert_before and redraw only the mutable tail (current streaming line, spinner, tool status) via Terminal::draw over a Viewport::Inline region; the tail MUST be freely redrawable each frame without disturbing committed scrollback."
  tui13,"xyevent-coverage","The TUI render MUST handle at minimum these XyEvent variants: TextDelta (stream to tail then commit on boundary), ThinkingDelta, ToolExecutionStart/Update/End, ModelSelect, Error, TurnStart/TurnEnd; unhandled variants MUST degrade gracefully (e.g. log) not panic."
  tui14,"slash-commands","The TUI MUST parse slash commands /exit (maps to Quit) and /model (maps to SetModel or CycleModel) reusing protocol::Command semantics; unknown slash input MUST show an inline error not crash."
  tui15,"terminal-lifecycle","The TUI MUST enable raw mode and Viewport::Inline on entry and MUST restore the terminal on exit via Drop or explicit teardown even on panic or error, so the user's terminal is never left in a broken raw-mode state."
  tui20,"core-backend-direct","The TUI MUST depend on ratatui-core and ratatui-crossterm directly (NOT the umbrella ratatui crate); the umbrella ratatui dependency MUST be removed from Cargo.toml. Evidence: ratatui-core v0.1.2 contains all types used (Terminal/Frame/Viewport::Inline/insert_before/set_cursor_position/Buffer/Layout/Style/Text/Line/Span/Widget trait) at ratatui/ratatui-core/src/; umbrella init.rs convenience (try_init_with_options/restore/DefaultTerminal) is ~15 lines replicated locally. ratatui-crossterm provides CrosstermBackend (ratatui/ratatui-crossterm/src/lib.rs:160)."
  tui21,"widget-usage-policy","The TUI MUST NOT be constrained to hand-rolled cell loops: ratatui-widgets (the independent crate, NOT the umbrella ratatui) is an allowed dependency, and its subset (Paragraph/Block/List/ListState/Clear) MAY be reused when it fits. When a library widget does not meet the inline-rendering need (e.g. a specific CJK/emoji behavior, or a custom interaction), the TUI MAY instead build a self-contained widget on top of ratatui-core primitives (Buffer/Layout/Style/Text/Widget trait). The umbrella ratatui crate MUST remain absent (see tui20). The choice between reuse and self-build MUST be driven by fit, not by a blanket prohibition."
  tui22,"scrolling-regions","The TUI MUST enable the ratatui-core scrolling-regions feature (forwarded via ratatui-crossterm) to reduce insert_before flicker; this addresses the c340 §7 known-leftover insert_before jelly effect."
  tui30,"user-message-echo","The TUI MUST commit the user's submitted prompt text to the scrollback immediately on Enter (before or during driver.run), styled distinctly (e.g. ❯ prefix) so the user sees their own message in the conversation history. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #3 noted user input never reached scrollback; pi/kimi-code user-message components (kimi-code/apps/kimi-code/src/tui/components/messages/user-message.ts) echo user input on submit."
  tui31,"turn-end-flush-consistent","The TUI MUST flush the final streaming line to scrollback and clear the tail in the same frame on TurnEnd, so no reply text lingers in the mutable tail after a turn completes. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #4 noted the last reply line stayed in the tail until the next submit."
  tui32,"input-anchored-visual","The TUI input region MUST appear visually anchored to the bottom (no floating/gap错觉); unused tail rows MUST be filled (background block or divider) so the input area reads as a continuous bottom-anchored region. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #1 noted Viewport::Inline(3) left a perceived gap; kimi-code footer uses background fill."
  tui40,"panic-hook-restore","The TUI MUST install a std::panic::set_hook before entering the inline viewport that restores the terminal (disable raw mode + restore) before chaining to the original hook, so the terminal is never left broken even under panic=abort or when a panic occurs in a spawned task whose stack has no InlineTerminal. Drop alone is insufficient: it does not run under panic=abort, and a panic in a spawn_blocking/spawn child task unwinds that child's stack (no InlineTerminal there). Evidence: codex tui.rs installs a panic hook for terminal restore; Rust's set_hook still executes under panic=abort whereas Drop does not."
  tui41,"render-test-coverage","The TUI rendering layer MUST be covered by TestBackend-based tests (ratatui_core::backend::TestBackend) that assert buffer content via assert_buffer_lines, covering at minimum: the draw_tail_frame path (empty and streaming states), the commit_to_scrollback insert_before path (including CJK double-width line commit), streaming text wrapping at terminal width, and TurnEnd tail flush. This replaces implementation-bound hand-written unit tests with behavior-level render assertions. Evidence: codex uses TestBackend + insta snapshots (codex-rs/tui snapshots/, docs/tui-research/codex.md §3); ratatui official tests use TestBackend + Viewport::Inline + insert_before (ratatui/tests/terminal.rs:66); the prior commit_to_scrollback cell loop (terminal.rs:86-119) had zero test coverage."
  tui42,"render-business-decoupling","The TUI rendering layer MUST be decoupled from the agent data/business flow: rendering functions MUST consume UI-only data types (e.g. a RenderedLine enum: UserInput/AssistantText/ToolSummary/Status) rather than domain XyEvent variants directly. The boundary between the UI/UX layer and the data-flow/business-flow layer MUST be explicit: business events (XyEvent) are translated into UI data types at a single seam, and the rendering layer MUST NOT match on XyEvent variants or call Driver/agent methods. Evidence: the current render::commit_lines_for (src/app/tui/render.rs:119) and app::handle_xy_event (src/app/tui/app.rs:102) mix XyEvent handling with line production, coupling rendering to the domain event vocabulary; codex isolates via HistoryCell (codex-rs/tui/src/history_cell/) and pi via typed message parts (packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/assistant-message.ts)."
  tui50,"streaming-mutable-last-line","The TUI streaming render MUST grow the in-progress (not-yet-newline-terminated) text in the mutable last line at the top of the tail region (visually continuous with the scrollback above), rendered within the ratatui buffer (inline viewport), NOT via direct terminal escape-sequence writes that bypass the ratatui buffer. Complete newline-terminated lines MUST be committed incrementally to the scrollback via insert_before as soon as their newline boundary arrives (not batched until turn end). The tail region MUST contain only: the mutable last line (top, redrawn each frame in the buffer, transparent background so it blends into the scrollback), the thinking/status indicator, and the input prompt (bottom). The mutable last line MUST wrap to multiple rows when it exceeds the terminal width (honoring CJK display width); rows beyond the tail capacity are dropped from the top (content is not lost — it commits to scrollback on the next newline). TurnEnd MUST flush any residual un-terminated text to the scrollback. The newline-gated buffer (drain_complete_lines on newline, pending_tail for the un-terminated remainder) is the core mechanism, modeled on codex MarkdownStreamCollector in simplified form (no markdown parsing, no table holdback, no animation chunking). Evidence: the escape-sequence implementation (raw_render.rs) had committed and mutable lines both write physical row viewport_top-1, overwriting each other, and TurnEnd clear_mutable erased committed content (the reply-cleared-after-stream bug); codex StreamController grows the active cell in place each frame within the buffer."
  tui51,"render-layer-componentized","The TUI rendering layer MUST be decomposed into reusable, self-contained widgets under the tui components directory, each consuming only UI-only data types (RenderedLine, a string, spinner index, input buffer), each independently verifiable via a TestBackend, and each composable by a layout widget (Tail) that bottom-anchors its children. At minimum: TranscriptLine (RenderedLine into Buffer for the insert_before commit path), MutableLine (pending tail at tail buffer top, wrapped, transparent bg), ThinkingIndicator (spinner plus label), InputPrompt (prompt plus input plus cursor plus input_bg block, CJK-aware cursor), Tail (composes the above, bottom-anchored, capacity-aware top-drop). draw_tail_frame MUST delegate to Tail render; commit_to_scrollback MUST consume a slice of RenderedLine and render via TranscriptLine. The rendering layer MUST NOT use direct terminal escape-sequence writes (raw escape or DECSTBM scroll-region manipulation) that bypass the ratatui buffer — such code is not widget-able (bound to physical coordinates), not TestBackend-verifiable (violates tui41), and bypasses the RenderedLine seam (violates tui42). Evidence: user goal that every TUI part be an explainable, reusable, individually-verifiable widget (component); the escape route (raw_render.rs) was the one non-widget-able part and produced the reply-cleared bug."
  tui52,"multi-round-turn-not-truncated","The TUI MUST drain the agent XyEvent stream for a user prompt until the stream ends (returns None) and MUST NOT stop at the first XyEvent::TurnEnd. The react loop emits one TurnEnd per ReAct iteration; a tool-calling turn spans multiple iterations (the model calls a tool then continues in a later iteration) so intermediate TurnEnds are single-iteration boundaries not the end of the whole user turn. The turn-fully-done signal (when to clear the mutable tail and reset streaming state) MUST be stream termination (None) delivered as an explicit end-of-stream message to the main loop, NOT a mid-stream TurnEnd. Evidence: spawn_drain broke on the first TurnEnd so tool-calling turns had their continuation events dropped and the REPL appeared to hang after a tool call; print mode consumes the whole stream via while-let-Some and is unaffected, confirming the multi-TurnEnd protocol is by design and the bug is TUI-side."
scenarios[34]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui1,"inline-viewport",the TUI source is inspected,"Viewport::Inline is used and insert_before commits finalized lines",no EnterAlternateScreen/?1049h is emitted and history remains in the terminal scrollback
  tui1,"scrollback-copy",a conversation turn finishes in the TUI,the user scrolls up in the terminal,prior turns are visible in the native scrollback and selectable with the terminal native selection
  tui2,"inprocess-default",xylitol is launched with no prompt and stdin is a TTY,the TUI starts,the agent is driven via InProcessDriver not RemoteDriver
  tui3,"rpc-retained",the rpc surface is inspected after the TUI lands,"--rpc dispatch and src/app/rpc.rs are checked",rpc mode is still present and functional
  tui3,"server-retained",the server surface is inspected after the TUI lands,xylitol server run and src/app/server are checked,the server is still present and functional
  tui4,"no-infra-import",the TUI source is inspected,imports under src/app/tui are checked,"none import crate::agent::session crate::agent::runtime or crate::infra and slash commands map to protocol::Command"
  tui5,"driven-on-land",a file is added under src/app/tui,it is checked at change completion,"it is reachable from tui::run and has no #[allow(dead_code)]"
  tui10,"tty-default",xylitol is run with no arguments and stdin is a TTY,the process starts,"app::tui::run is entered and an inline REPL is shown"
  tui10,"prompt-stays-print",xylitol 'fix the bug' is run,the process starts,print mode runs (not the TUI) because a prompt was given
  tui11,"abort-on-cancel",a long agent turn is streaming,the user presses the cancel key,"Driver::abort is called and the loop breaks cleanly"
  tui12,"scrollback-commit",a finalized text line exists,insert_before is called,the line appears in the terminal scrollback above the live viewport and is not redrawn on subsequent frames
  tui13,"textdelta-stream",a TextDelta event arrives,the tail is redrawn,the partial text is visible in the tail region and on a newline boundary is committed to scrollback
  tui13,"tool-status",a ToolExecutionStart then ToolExecutionEnd occur,the events are rendered,tool name and result preview appear without panicking
  tui14,"exit-command",the user types /exit,the command is parsed,the REPL exits cleanly restoring the terminal
  tui14,"model-command",the user types /model,the user types /model,"the model is switched via protocol::Command SetModel/CycleModel semantics"
  tui15,"restore-on-panic",the TUI panics during a turn,the panic unwinds,raw mode is disabled and the terminal is usable
  tui20,"no-umbrella-dep",Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are inspected after the change,dependency names are checked,"ratatui 0.30.x is absent and ratatui-core + ratatui-crossterm are present"
  tui21,"widget-choice-driven-by-fit",a TUI rendering path needs to display wrapped text or a bordered box,the implementation is chosen,"either a ratatui-widgets subset (Paragraph/Block) is reused OR a self-contained widget is built on ratatui-core primitives and neither choice is blocked by a blanket prohibition"
  tui21,"umbrella-still-absent",Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are inspected after the change,dependency names are checked,"the umbrella ratatui crate is absent while ratatui-core and ratatui-crossterm remain (and ratatui-widgets may be present)"
  tui22,"flicker-reduced",a long streaming turn with frequent TextDelta newlines is rendered in the TUI,the terminal is observed,"insert_before commits do not produce visible clear-and-redraw jelly effect (scrolling-regions engaged)"
  tui30,"user-input-visible",the user types a prompt and presses Enter,the scrollback is inspected,the user's prompt text appears as a committed line above the live tail region
  tui31,"no-tail-linger",a streaming turn reaches TurnEnd,the frame after TurnEnd is rendered,the tail contains no leftover assistant text from the finished turn and the final line is in scrollback
  tui32,"no-floating-input",the TUI is idle with an empty input,the tail region is observed,the input area is visually anchored to the bottom edge with no ambiguous gap above it
  tui40,"panic-hook-installed-before-viewport",the TUI source is inspected,the run() entry point is read,"install_terminal_restore_hook is called before InlineTerminal::enter"
  tui40,"panic-abort-still-restores",the process is built with panic=abort and the TUI panics during a turn,the panic hook fires,raw mode is disabled and the terminal is usable before the process terminates
  tui41,"render-harness-covers-commit",commit_to_scrollback renders a CJK line via insert_before,the TestBackend buffer is asserted,"the double-width characters occupy two columns and the assertion uses assert_buffer_lines not per-cell hand-rolled checks"
  tui42,"no-xyevent-in-render",the TUI rendering functions are inspected,their input types are checked,"they consume UI-only data types (e.g. RenderedLine) and no rendering function matches on XyEvent variants or calls Driver/agent methods"
  tui50,"complete-lines-commit-incrementally",a TextDelta containing a newline arrives during a turn,the event is handled,the complete line before the newline is committed to scrollback immediately via insert_before (not held until TurnEnd)
  tui50,"pending-tail-grows-in-tail-top",streaming text without a newline is arriving,the tail frame is rendered each frame,"the un-terminated text appears in the top row of the tail region (mutable last line) growing in place within the ratatui buffer and the thinking indicator sits below it and the input prompt at the bottom"
  tui51,"widgets-independently-testable",each widget under the tui components directory is exercised,it is rendered to a TestBackend buffer and asserted,"TranscriptLine, MutableLine, ThinkingIndicator, InputPrompt, Tail each render their expected content independently without a real terminal"
  tui51,"no-escape-direct-write","the tui source is inspected for escape-sequence rendering","raw_render.rs and any DECSTBM or MoveTo-then-Print bypass of the ratatui buffer are checked","no escape-sequence direct-write rendering path exists; all rendering goes through the ratatui buffer"
  tui52,"tool-turn-continuation-reaches-tui",a turn runs a tool call then the model produces a final text reply across multiple ReAct iterations,the XyEvent stream is drained by the TUI and rendered,the final text reply after the tool call is rendered in the TUI (not dropped) and the mutable tail reflects the continuation
  tui52,"drain-breaks-on-stream-end",the TUI drain task is inspected,the stream consumption loop is read,the loop breaks on stream None or external cancellation and does NOT break on an intermediate TurnEnd
  tui52,"tail-cleared-on-stream-end","a multi-iteration tool-calling turn finishes",the stream returns None,the mutable tail is cleared and streaming state is reset exactly once when the stream ends (not on the intermediate TurnEnd that precedes the continuation round)
